  "term": "brainwave entrainment",
  "definition": "Brainwave entrainment is the idea that rhythmic external stimulation can cause the brain’s electrical activity to synchronize with the same frequency. In this packet, it is discussed mainly in relation to binaural beats, but the reviewed evidence for such entrainment effects is described as inconsistent.",
